		<blockquote class=3D"mycode_quote"><cite><span> (10-08-2023, 09:59 PM)</s=
pan>codycbradio Wrote:  <a href=3D"https://www.hpmuseum.org/forum/post-1782=
09.html#pid178209" class=3D"quick_jump"></a></cite>Does anybody know how to=
 calculate the different electrical units with a given set of other units i=
n Plus42?</blockquote><br>
Pretty much the same way you do other units.<br>
Using the simplest example (length):<br>
[Units] [Leng]<br>
10 [enter]<br>
[m]  =3D&gt; (results in) 10_m on stack<br>
1 [enter]<br>
[in] =3D&gt; 1_in (in x register), 10_m (in y register).<br>
[f] [UNIT.FCN] [Conv]<br>
x: 393.7_in<br>
<br>
Just make sure your units are compatible.  <br>
Farads are not convertible to Newton-meters per second squared.<br>
<br>
Hope this helps!
	</div>
